comdlg32: XDG desktop portal file dialogs (off by default).

Ported from NickPittas' AE4Linux (LGPL-2.1+, permission in AdobeWine issue #2), which carried a
capture of Wine merge request 10060 (patches/wine/comdlg32/xdg-portal-base.patch, "provisional")
and its own FORCE rule (force-portal-no-native-fallback.patch, "accepted behavior").
Upstream: https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/10060 by Alexander Wilms
<f.alexander.wilms@outlook.com>, "comdlg32: Use XDG Desktop Portal for native file dialogs",
draft, closed unmerged by its author on 2026-08-27; not in any Wine release up to 11.18. This is
based on the MR's last revision (head f36314a5), newer than AE4Linux's capture (shared
wine/appdefaults.h helper, NULL lpstrFile checks): its first two commits, 35be6a5b "comdlg32: add
XDG desktop portal backend for file dialogs" and 23c832a0 "comdlg32: route IFileDialog through
portal when compatible". Not taken: the winecfg policy page, the FOS_PICKFOLDERS test and the
shell32 SHBrowseForFolderW routing.

GetOpenFileName/GetSaveFileName (A and W) and IFileOpenDialog/IFileSaveDialog ask
org.freedesktop.portal.FileChooser over D-Bus (libdbus is dlopen'ed by comdlg32.so) and convert the
returned file:// URIs to DOS paths. Policy, from WINE_FORCE_PORTAL or the registry value
HKCU\Software\Wine\X11 Driver\FileDialogPortal (also per app under AppDefaults\<exe>\X11 Driver):
  WINE_FORCE_PORTAL=1 or "always": every file dialog goes to the portal
  "auto": only dialogs without hooks, templates, custom controls or event handlers
  WINE_FORCE_PORTAL=0, "never" or nothing set: Wine's own dialogs, as before
Changes against the MR: off unless enabled (the MR defaulted to auto); comdlg32.so is loaded on the
first portal request instead of in DllMain; the request buffers (~190 KB) are allocated only when
the portal is used instead of on the stack of every GetOpenFileNameW/GetSaveFileNameW call; the
MR's whitespace-only changes are dropped. Nick's FORCE rule: when the portal was reached but
failed, FORCE does not silently open Wine's dialog instead (IFileDialog::Show returns the error;
for the legacy calls the same is done here, returning FALSE with CDERR_DIALOGFAILURE, while a
missing D-Bus/portal service still falls back). WoW64 (32-bit apps) has no thunks and keeps
Wine's dialogs.

